id: pm-gantt-chart-2u8i
title: Coverage gate excludes executable tooling and the merge-driver hook is JavaScript
description: "The 100 percent gate walks coverageGate.sources=[\".\"] but DEFAULT_SKIP_DIRS excludes scripts, so scripts/coverage-gate.ts, scripts/docstring-gate.ts, and scripts/prepare-merge-driver.mjs are outside the measured source set. The last file is executable JavaScript despite the fleet TypeScript-only requirement. Existing index.ts coverage remains exact, but the package cannot honestly claim all-source 100/100/100/100 until tooling is migrated, independently tested, included in the measured inventory, and statement-equivalent coverage is explicitly reported or justified by the runtime."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: code-quality,coverage,fleet-mandate,typescript
created_at: "2026-08-17T05:12:53.979Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T08:46:24.537Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Replace executable .mjs with erasable TypeScript or an approved zero-logic launcher; measure every package-owned executable TypeScript source including gate scripts; enforce exact lines branches functions and an explicit statement-equivalence contract; negative controls prove a new untested root or scripts source fails; release check and fresh install pass
risk: high
severity: high
expected_result: "Every executable package-owned source file is TypeScript, enumerated by the exact coverage inventory, independently tested, and gated at exact coverage without ignores or source exclusions."
actual_result: "Configured index.ts coverage is exact, but four executable tooling files are outside measurement, one is JavaScript, 62 test lines use explicit any, and the release gate lacks ESLint and jscpd."
